From ae2347f0c6272a9832806e17d3a5c47f437030aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:57:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: Describe the SMC's second
 GPIO bank

The T6050 SMC has a second bank of GPIO keys, the lower-case gp keys,
as T6030 and T6031 do; on the J716s macsmc-low-gpio finds gp01 as its
first key. gpio-macsmc drives it as "apple,smc-low-gpio", and the MFD
core registers the bank only when this child node exists.

Describe it next to the other SMC children as "gpio-low", the node name
apple,smc.yaml documents and t6041-j616c.dts uses, with the label the
T6030 and T6031 files use. The J716s trackpad's AFE reset is on it
(gp1c).

Tested on J716s.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
index 86eaef24e98f..3c136b3692f5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
@@ -94,6 +94,17 @@ smc: smc@28c600000 {
 		reg-names = "smc", "sram";
 		mboxes = <&smc_mbox>;
 
+		/*
+		 * The SMC's second GPIO bank: the lower-case gp keys (gp01 on), next to the
+		 * gP keys of the first, as on T6030/T6031. The J716s trackpad's AFE reset is
+		 * gp1c (line 28).
+		 */
+		smc_gpio_low: gpio-low {
+			compatible = "apple,smc-low-gpio";
+			gpio-controller;
+			#gpio-cells = <2>;
+		};
+
 		/* T8142's key discovery (every readable T* float key); boards add their fan and power keys. */
 		smc_hwmon: hwmon {
 			compatible = "apple,smc-hwmon";
-- 
